    {
      "id": "c17-l3",
      "title": "Insert and Remove",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "To insert after a node p: the new node points to p's next, then p points to the new node. Two pointer changes, no shifting of elements like in an array.",
        "To remove a node, the node before it must skip it: prev->next = victim->next; then free(victim). Removing the head is special: the head itself moves on.",
        "When you're done with a list, free every node. Save next before freeing, because after free you can't read it anymore."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "#include <stdio.h>",
          "#include <stdlib.h>",
          "",
          "struct node {",
          "    int value;",
          "    struct node *next;",
          "};",
          "",
          "struct node *push(struct node *head, int v) {",
          "    struct node *n = malloc(sizeof(struct node));",
          "    n->value = v;",
          "    n->next = head;",
          "    return n;",
          "}",
          "",
          "struct node *removev(struct node *head, int v) {",
          "    struct node *p = head, *prev = NULL;",
          "    while (p != NULL && p->value != v) {",
          "        prev = p;",
          "        p = p->next;",
          "    }",
          "    if (p == NULL) return head;",
          "    if (prev == NULL) head = p->next;",
          "    else prev->next = p->next;",
          "    free(p);",
          "    return head;",
          "}",
          "",
          "int main() {",
          "    struct node *head = NULL, *p, *next;",
          "    int i;",
          "    for (i = 4; i >= 1; i--)",
          "        head = push(head, i);",
          "    head = removev(head, 3);",
          "    head = removev(head, 1);",
          "    for (p = head; p != NULL; p = p->next)",
          "        printf(\"%d \", p->value);",
          "    printf(\"\\n\");",
          "    for (p = head; p != NULL; p = next) {",
          "        next = p->next;",
          "        free(p);",
          "    }",
          "    return 0;",
          "}"
        ],
        "output": [
          "2 4 "
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "c17-l3-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
